      "children": [
        {
          "texts": [
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.27 improves performance of small allocations using size-specialized allocation functions."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.27 includes new goroutine leak profiles."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.27 adds generic methods—a highly desired language feature."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.27 adds generic methods, encoding/json/v2 package, uuid package, faster memory allocation, goroutine leak profiles, and more."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Introducing the new programmatic API for pkg.go.dev, allowing developers to fetch package and module data directly."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.26 simplifies type construction and enhances cycle detection for certain kinds of recursive types."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "How Go 1.26's source-level inliner works, and how it can help you with self-service API migrations."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "A description of some of the recent changes to do allocations on the stack instead of the heap."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.26 includes a new implementation of go fix that can help you use more modern features of Go."
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "value": "Go 1.26 adds a new garbage collector, cgo overhead reduction, experimental simd/archsimd package, experimental runtime/secret package, and more."
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "value": "Opens in new window."
